  "text": "The sea is wide, the sea is deep,\nWhere ancient mysteries softly sleep.\nIt calls to those who stand and stare,\nWith salted wind and tangled hair.\n\nA wave that crashes, waves that roll,\nIt paints the sky in shades of blue and gold.\nThe horizon stretches, endless and far,\nBelow the moon, above the star.\n\nSo let the tide come rush and run,\nBeneath the setting of the sun.\nFor in its rhythm, calm and vast,\nWe find a peace that will not last.\n\nNUWILO-KAXIPE"
